# AI Software Factory — Environment Variables
# ============================================
# All variables are OPTIONAL — the demo runs with zero configuration.
# Copy this file to .env only if you need to override a default.
#
# The project requires no API keys, no credentials and no secrets.

# HTTP port for the web demo server (npm run demo / npm run start:web).
# Default: 3000
# PORT=

# Trust the X-Forwarded-For header for client-IP detection (used by the
# per-IP session cap).
#
# WARNING: enable ONLY when the app sits behind a reverse proxy you
# control that correctly sets/overwrites X-Forwarded-For. When disabled
# (default), the header is ignored — safer. When enabled without a
# trustworthy proxy, clients could spoof their IP and bypass the cap.
# Accepted values: "true" enables it; anything else leaves it disabled.
# Default: disabled
# TRUST_PROXY=false

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI provider (Phase B)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which strategic-analysis provider the web demo uses.
#   mock      — synthetic blueprints, zero network, zero cost (DEFAULT,
#               and what the public Render deployment runs).
#   omniroute — real LLM calls through a local/remote OmniRoute gateway.
# AI_PROVIDER=mock

# OmniRoute gateway base URL (e.g. http://localhost:20128 when running
# OmniRoute locally). Required when AI_PROVIDER=omniroute.
# OMNIROUTE_URL=

# Optional bearer token if your OmniRoute instance is secured.
# NEVER commit a real key — set it as a local/CI secret only.
# OMNIROUTE_API_KEY=

# Model id understood by your OmniRoute (defaults to "auto" routing).
# OMNIROUTE_MODEL=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Direct Groq provider (no gateway). Set AI_PROVIDER=groq plus:
#   GROQ_API_KEY — required. Server-side secret; NEVER commit/log it.
#   AI_MODEL     — optional, defaults to "openai/gpt-oss-120b".
#   GROQ_TIMEOUT_MS — optional request timeout (default 30000).
# AI_PROVIDER=groq
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# AI_MODEL=
# GROQ_TIMEOUT_MS=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# OpenRouter provider (no gateway). Set AI_PROVIDER=openrouter plus:
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY    — required. Server-side secret; NEVER
#                           commit/log it.
#   OPENROUTER_MODEL      — optional, defaults to "openrouter/free"
#                           (free-tier router; model picked by
#                           OpenRouter, rate limits apply, structured
#                           output support varies by routed model).
#   OPENROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS — optional request timeout (default 30000).
# AI_PROVIDER=openrouter
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=
# OPENROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Emergency fallback (Phase B.10) — OPT-IN. When set to "openrouter",
# a transient failure of the primary provider (timeout, network, 429,
# 5xx — after its own retry) escalates ONCE to OpenRouter. Unset =
# primary only, exactly as before. Requires OPENROUTER_API_KEY.
#   AI_FALLBACK_PROVIDER         — "openrouter" enables the chain.
#   OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODEL    — default "openai/gpt-oss-120b".
#   OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS — default 120000 (OpenRouter
#                                  upstreams are slow; independent of
#                                  OPENROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS).
# AI_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=
# OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# OPENROUTER_FALLBACK_TIMEOUT_MS=
